**A child re-renders whenever its parent does, whatever the props are.** That is the default. `React.memo` is what turns it off.

Then `memo` compares props by identity. Objects, arrays and arrow functions built during render are brand new each time. So they never match, and `memo` gives you nothing.

```jsx
const Child = memo(function Child({ data, onClick }) { /* ... */ })

const data = useMemo(() => ({ id }), [id])
const onClick = useCallback(() => save(id), [id])
```

Two more traps. JSX passed as `children` is a new element every render. And any context the child reads will re-render it regardless of props.
